#!/usr/bin/env bash
# RETIRED with the Salapify 2 archive, 2026-09-18, on founder direction.
#
# This hook used to refuse a push that would ship a Shorebird patch under a
# stamp already recorded in docs/delivery-log.md. It only ever mattered because
# a push touching flutter/ eventually reached main and shipped to the founder's
# phone. flutter/ now lives at archive/salapify-2-flutter/ and its publisher
# workflows are disabled, so there is no stamp, no patch and nothing to collide
# with.
#
# It is written out rather than deleted because the check itself was sound and
# caught three real collisions (docs/lunch-and-learn.md, sessions 32 and 33).
# The script it called is preserved at
#   archive/salapify-2-flutter/ci-disabled/scripts/check-stamp-unique.sh
# and this hook's previous body is in this file's git history. If Salapify 2 is
# ever un-archived, restore both together; a publisher without this guard is
# how the collisions happened in the first place.
#
# The reason this file still exists at all, saying so out loud, is that the
# previous version would have gone SILENT rather than absent: its first act was
#   if [ ! -f flutter/lib/main.dart ]; then exit 0; fi
# which the archive move satisfies. A guard that exits 0 while its subject has
# moved reads exactly like a guard that ran and passed. This repository has
# been bitten by that shape before.
set -euo pipefail

exit 0
